WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:07.288
First: a policy is assigned to a group
that contains a Tier 1 service principal.

3
00:00:07.288 --> 00:00:08.299
What happens?

4
00:00:08.299 --> 00:00:09.525
The answer is b.

5
00:00:09.525 --> 00:00:11.887
It isn't enforced for
the service principal.

6
00:00:11.887 --> 00:00:16.200
Microsoft Learn's Conditional
Access for workload identities page

7
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.512
says to assign it directly, by the
enterprise application's object I D.

8
00:00:20.512 --> 00:00:23.417
Second: a new C A oh
thirty-seven policy is

9
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:26.762
created on the same run
that enforces its ring.

10
00:00:26.762 --> 00:00:28.625
What state is it created in?

11
00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:30.937
The answer is b: report-only.

12
00:00:30.937 --> 00:00:33.393
Every policy is created report-only,

13
00:00:33.393 --> 00:00:37.076
whatever its ring's state, and
it turns on in the next run.

14
00:00:37.076 --> 00:00:39.502
The module page has three more questions,

15
00:00:39.502 --> 00:00:42.050
each linked to the
section that answers it.
